Read the guidance index first: [openrouter-chat guidance](../../../docs/guidance/openrouter-chat/index.md). Each reference covers one area; open the ones for the paths you touch.

| Changing | Read |
| --- | --- |
| The chat route, streaming, tools, structured output | [ai-sdk](../../../docs/guidance/openrouter-chat/ai-sdk.md), [openrouter](../../../docs/guidance/openrouter-chat/openrouter.md) |
| Provider options, the models list, attribution | [openrouter](../../../docs/guidance/openrouter-chat/openrouter.md), `docs/openrouter.md` |
| Components, pages, styling | [ui](../../../docs/guidance/openrouter-chat/ui.md), [styling](../../../docs/guidance/openrouter-chat/styling.md), [design-slop](../../../docs/guidance/openrouter-chat/design-slop.md), `DESIGN.md` |
| Rate limits and stream slots | [rate-limiting](../../../docs/guidance/openrouter-chat/rate-limiting.md) |
| Tests, fixtures, evals | [testing](../../../docs/guidance/openrouter-chat/testing.md) |
| A new route, service or tool | [workflows](../../../docs/guidance/openrouter-chat/workflows.md) |

The rules that hold everywhere:

- Effect owns everything before the stream and the AI SDK owns the stream. Every failure before the stream is an HTTP error with `{ message, retryable }` through `runRoute`.
- Components never import Effect or anything under `app/.server/`.
- Tests never reach the network. The only fakes are third parties: the AI SDK mock model and the shipped stub OpenRouter in `tests/helpers/stub-openrouter.ts`. Never mock the app's own modules.
- Read the installed `ai` and `@openrouter/ai-sdk-provider` type declarations before using an API; names move between majors.
- `bun run eval` calls the real API and costs money. It never runs in tests or CI.

Before calling work done, follow [verification](../../../docs/guidance/openrouter-chat/verification.md): `bun run check`, read the counts, then run the app with `bun run dev:bg` and exercise the change once.

The Claude-only TypeScript hooks aren't installed for this agent, so keep the same boundaries through the project linter and tests.
